      "seed": 261121011,
      "endpoint": "/create-image-pro-flash",
      "prompt": "Native low-resolution sprite material for a high top-down orthographic city game. Seven separated little asymmetrical grass tufts, some narrow and some wider. Make each tuft from three to seven rooted curved blades. Match the supplied screenshot's organic fine blade structure and rich golden yellow against muted yellow-olive at the feet. Every grass blade is individually visible, traced with one pixel thick stepped curved lines, rooted together at low olive bases. Vary blade height from 3 to 7 pixels and lean all blades at slightly different angles. Uneven outward crescents and the occasional single bright seed-tip pixel show an active meadow. Add greenish ochre to the lower half, straw gold to upper shafts, and tiny cream-yellow bright tips on only a few blades. Keep the blade segments crisp discrete pixels with clean transparency, no stroke outline, blur, airbrush, black pixels, bulky bright feet, fallen leaves, flowers, wheat or farm crops. On a transparent 48x48 canvas, retain transparent gaps between tufts. Render only the grass, the transparent ground will receive the game's normal grass texture.",
